      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5de9405aea7cc52772fcc359|full_name}: Everything that relies on correct bone position data or tracking data doesn't work correct, unless done in PostLateUpdate. Especially for FBT users. For example, the armature can be stretched for some reasons, and bone positions can be somewhere else, but not where the player is. Teleport completey breaks randomly when done during OnDeserialization (e.g. when receiving an event) and not during Update, e.g. it can move the camera away from the player, the avatar can get stuck on a collider, UI can break etc. (I can't find my own canny about this bug, but this here describes the same issue: https://vrchat.canny.io/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-bugs/p/teleportation-issues)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-08-08T13:25:02.977Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When you send a network event, the receiver will execute it during OnDeserialization. A lot of stuff causes bugs when done at this event timing, so we need to delay the event on the receiving side ourselves with extra code to avoid issues. \nIt would be good if Udon would have an option to already only execute the remote call on the receiving side during a specified EventTiming.",
